===Season format===
The regular season runs from December through March, avoiding overlap with the high school and university rugby seasons that form the foundation of Sanese rugby development. Teams play a round-robin format within their conference, followed by a playoff tournament culminating in the championship final.

The knockout phase of the season is known as the [[Emperor's Shield]] tournament, which determines the overall league champion. The Emperor's Shield final is one of the most-watched sporting events in Okaiken, routinely attracting television audiences exceeding 30 million viewers.

===Foreign player regulations===
League One maintains strict regulations on foreign player participation to ensure the development of domestic talent. Each team may field a maximum of three foreign players on the pitch simultaneously, with at least one required to be eligible for the Sanese national team. Additionally, one player from an [[Shendan Ocean]] rugby union (such as [[Yanbaru]] or [[Dagit]]) may take the field for each team, reflecting Okaiken's regional sporting ties.

